  "id": "COMPOUND:23954 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Fumiquinazoline B is implicated in the regulation of the High-affinity choline transporter through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Fumiquinazoline B acts as a target of multiple proteins, including Thioredoxin, Rhetsinine, and Pseudopterosin Q, all of which are involved in targeting the choline transporter. These proteins are part of a broader network of molecular pathways that modulate choline transport, likely through redox or signaling mechanisms. The consistent presence of the choline transporter as a target across different pathways indicates a potential role for Fumiquinazoline B in influencing choline transport activity, possibly by modulating the activity of these upstream proteins. The integration of these findings highlights a possible mechanism by which Fumiquinazoline B could exert its effects on choline transport, though the exact molecular pathway remains to be fully elucidated.",
